      <TableCell><code>chunkSizeMiB</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>integer</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>chunkSizeMiB defines the size of the multipart upload chunks of the S3 API. The S3 API requires multipart upload chunks to be at least 5MiB. When omitted, this means no opinion and the platform is left to choose a reasonable default, which is subject to change over time. The current default value is 10 MiB. The value is an integer number of MiB. The minimum value is 5 and the maximum value is 5120 (5 GiB).</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>cloudFront</code></TableCell>
